cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Verb∋Net, please cite the paper below."
type: dataset
title: "Verb∋Net: a VerbNet-style lexicon of French verbs"
version: 1.0.0
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
url: "https://aymara.github.io/verbenet/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aymara/verbenet"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23018909
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.23018909
    description: "Concept DOI of the dataset on Zenodo, which resolves to the latest version."
abstract: >-
  Verb∋Net is a French adaptation of VerbNet. Verbs are grouped into classes that share
  thematic roles with selectional restrictions and syntactic frames; each frame has an example
  and a semantic formula. It was built semi-automatically from VerbNet, Les Verbes Français and
  the Lexique-Grammaire, then revised by hand.
keywords:
  - VerbNet
  - French
  - lexicon
  - verb classes
  - semantic role labeling
